    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) and **Coby Mayo** (61.44), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable park factor and a manageable matchup against tough but exploitable arms. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a top-tier play at 65.74 despite the difficult assignment against Shane McClanahan; while his platoon edge is negative, the park factor and his elite role at the top of the order buoy his efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) and **Kyle Tucker** (58.24) represent our most consistent output in the outfield, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically highlighted for his secondary value in stealing bases, an area where we must capitalize given our strategic overweighting of speed.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Heliot Ramos**, who sat at a 45.34 efficiency. While **Heliot Ramos** offers intriguing stolen base potential against the slow delivery of Cease, his overall projected efficiency fell just short of the threshold required to displace starters like **Luis Robert Jr.** or **Andy Pages**. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Liam Hicks**, who carries a high efficiency of 57.76 but remains a risk if he drops lower than the 8th spot in the order. Furthermore, while **Wade Meckler** is active, he faces a negative platoon disadvantage against Cody Bradford; however, his elite sprint speed and leadoff role are deemed vital to our 5x5 objectives, forcing his inclusion despite the marginal 48.34 score.\n\nManagement remains cautious regarding the SP_xERA volatility today. Both **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Drake Baldwin** are facing high-caliber pitchers in Cease and Henderson, respectively, leading to tempered expectations. We are maintaining a strict watch on **Jordan Westburg** and **Jacob Wilson**, who remain on the IL, as our depth\u2014including assets like **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White**\u2014will need to be assessed if the current lineup underperforms relative to their daily floor. No significant weather-related delays are forecasted, but with several players positioned in high-wind zones, we are leaning into the 5% boost for **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** to provide extra-base hit potential in their favorable matchups against Christian Scott.",
